Goal:
The goal is to retrive the ssh private key for bandit26 using the scp command.

Connect:
ssh user@host -port

Approach:
. One part that confused me was remote-to-local and the vice-versa. [istg im not dumb :-( ]
. The command for the remote to local was pretty straightforward.

Command:
I. Remote → Local:
  scp username@remote_ip:/path/to/remote/file /path/to/local/destination

II. Local → Remote:
  scp /path/to/local/file username@remote_ip:/path/to/remote/destination

chmod 700 priv.key 
(This is very important as the ssh expects the private key to have strict permissions)

Breakdown:
The only important part is to set the permissoins for the private key file the syntax is easy
to interpret. we are connecting to a remote host and using the ssh protocol to copy the file 
onto our system.

Results:
I got the password after copying the private key.

Key-takeaway:
Learnt scp command and permissions settings for private.key file for ssh.
